s":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-b4.1","local_name":"sase-b4.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-b4","agent_clan_generation":"20260730071541","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-b4.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-b4[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Gate `@` reference file rows behind kind misses and explicit Ctrl+T[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The grouped `@` reference menu lists local file rows only when no [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]artifact kind prefix-matches the typed text, or when the user [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]explicitly asks for them (`Ctrl+T` in the ACE prompt, a manually [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]invoked completion request over LSP). The rule is decided once in [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the shared Rust core so the TUI and every LSP client agree.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]at_reference_file_row_gate.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-b4[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-b4/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared kind-stage file-row gate in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-gate: add an at-reference menu options wire plus a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`files_suppressed` menu flag to `sase_core`, suppress Kind-stage path [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows when an artifact kind prefix-matches the query unless the caller [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]opts in, expose the option through the `sase_core_rs` binding, and map [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]an `Invoked` LSP completion request to the opt-in.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE prompt gating and the Ctrl+T reveal[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-gate: thread the new menu option through the Python artifact-ref [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]facade and prompt completion mixins, add a per-menu \"files revealed\" [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state that a first `Ctrl+T` press sets instead of force-completing, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]surface a `[^T] files` panel hint, and refresh the affected tests and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Raise the sase-core-rs floor and verify end to end[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #5FD7AF] xsmall [/bold black on #5FD7AF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-floor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-gate, tui-gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-floor: raise the published `sase-core-rs` dependency window in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`pyproject.toml` to the release that carries the gate, then run the full[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repo check and confirm the behavior against the published wheel.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-b4","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-b4.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-d96f20194f2189805f677e076b52f1a5","started_at":"2026-07-30T11:15:55.031606+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785414776,"sha":"11cdd7807bc30b10cbb073f1af7bb17060c0bfab","subject":"build(deps): require sase-core-rs 0.12.19"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"3bea213e4e78882f12e9af5debda89db22bd0e0ad344c2d7cfa3c50ffc8b8d02","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-b4.land--code/chat.md","size_bytes":8408},"commits":{"digest":"26d10e3d5954b38106959b05bdb3e5436b63a29450080386b32ea